en  take on a much bigger villain last but  not least the tentacle monster gargantus  should be mentioned in the comics this  is a sea monster and an enemy of black  panther ii antagonist neymar since  gargantus has already appeared in both  trailers and as seen in the what if  series doesn't really pose much of a  threat we are not assuming a truly  relevant villain here i'm sure he will  be dangerous to doctor strange at one  moment or another but will probably be  dealt with by the protagonist during the  movie  as already seen in the second trailer we  will not be able to welcome wanda  maximov as a newcomer there's for  example an appearance of sir patrick  stewart as professor x as you can tell  from his unmistakable voice if you've  been paying close attention you'll have  noticed that captain marvel will also  make an appearance in doctor strange and  the multiverse of madness however it's  not the well-known carol danvers played  by bree larsen but monica rambo she is  played by teona paris and is the  daughter of carol's best friend rambo  already had her first appearance in one  division where it becomes clear that she  is captain marvel from another universe  and has already gained experience as a  superhero there the storyline is in line  with the marvel comics where rambo  succeeds denver's inner role as cap  marvel in the trailer she can be seen  fighting wanda so it remains exciting to  see how big the role of the new captain  marvel will be of course there are  several other characters who will make  an appearance in doctor strange and the  multiverse of madness among others  benedict wong as wong rachel mcadams as  christine palmer shoshil gomez is  america chavez as well as michael  stuhlbarg as nicodemus west  now we would like to introduce you to  another theory that has been circulating  for some time and that many marvel fans  wish would come true in the comics there  exists a gathering called the illuminati  this is originally a seven-member 